{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/265845-pack-question","id":265845,"title":"Pack question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-25T18:31:47-07:00","id":265845,"title":"Pack question","content":"I have a question could you make a pack to make some one immortal in the sense they don't age anymore and don't die from a gun shot to the head or something. Let say I want to make a deal with a human I give them that and they let say watch over something for me forever. Could I make a pack like that to make them immortal ?<br /> <br /> To keep in the theme with horror they don't heal anymore do any damage they get they keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 09-25-2014, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T19:18:35-07:00","id":265890,"title":"","content":"The word is Pact.<br /> <br /> And no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T19:21:38-07:00","id":265893,"title":"","content":"Beating the age problem is a question that I've said my piece on before, in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life\">this</a> thread. My answer to the damage question goes along similar lines:<br /> <br /> The ability to create invincible bodyguards who are magically indebted to you, at a cost equivalent to one night's good sleep or a single gambling binge per eternal meat shield, is a bit beyond what you have to offer on the raw power of a pact. Something similar could probably be accomplished in the form of an Exploit, but depending on whether it has drawbacks and how bad they might be, it's likely to require upkeep and continued investment by the demon rather than being able to fire and forget.<br /> <br /> From a dramatic standpoint, I wouldn't consider &quot;the human runs out of meat and eventually will be a miserable cupful of motionless viscera&quot; to be an appropriate balancing drawback. Aesthetically, the consequence probably fits a fleshier WoD game than Demon's information-age anxieties, but more importantly, there are many Unchained for whom this would not be a drawback at all. Tricked a human being into ruining their own life and dooming themselves to a miserable purgatory from which there is no escape: totally worth it, got a great catspaw that doesn't suffer compromises and will last for a few missions. Conversely, Unchained who would care about the welfare of their loved ones, while they'd be making a bad deal in the long run unless they found some other way to restore damage done, would still get an easy deal that would provide great protection to everyone they want to protect on a time-scale that might cover an entire chronicle's length if they're careful, deflating tension and killing plot hooks without leaving much in their place.<br /> <br /> More interesting drawbacks would probably both be subtler and weigh on the demon as well, such as some form of shared vulnerability, Cover-damaging glitches that grow more severe until the human receives sufficient medical attention to restore them to a normally viable state, or identity issues that cause the demon's psyche to blur with and overwhelm the human's, until they're little more than a weak, independently mobile Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}